# Closed-loop auditory stimulation in phase with sleep slow-oscillation up states (Ngo et al. 2013)
#
# A published sensory stimulation protocol, encoded from its source with
# SSTIM terms. It describes the method as the source reports it and asserts
# no effect: evidence about effects is a separate, authored claim (ADR 0027).
# The protocol cites its paper with dct:source instead of naming a framework
# (ADR 0064), its skos:editorialNote says what was read, and a level the
# source reports without a measurement point keeps the source's words in
# sstim:reportedAs at an unstated stage (ADR 0063). Why these protocols exist
# and how they are read: static/ontology/instances/README.md.

@prefix bfo:             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_> .
@prefix obo:             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .
@prefix dct:             <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix prov:            <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs:            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix sstim:           <https://w3id.org/sstim#> .
@prefix sstim-ex:        <https://w3id.org/sstim/exposure#> .
@prefix sstim-v:         <https://w3id.org/sstim/vocab#> .
@prefix sstim-ref:       <https://w3id.org/sstim/ref/> .
@prefix xsd:             <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix bsclab-protocol: <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/protocol/> .
@prefix n2013:           <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/protocol/ngo-2013-closed-loop-auditory-slow-oscillation#> .


###########################################################################
# 7. Ngo, Martinetz, Born and Mölle 2013: closed-loop auditory stimulation
#    of the sleep slow oscillation. Full text: Experimental Procedures.
###########################################################################

bsclab-protocol:ngo-2013-closed-loop-auditory-slow-oscillation a sstim:SensoryStimulationProtocol ;
    rdfs:label "Closed-loop auditory stimulation in phase with sleep slow-oscillation up states (Ngo et al. 2013)"@en ;
    dct:description "Sleeping adults hear two 50 ms bursts of pink noise each time their frontal EEG crosses a threshold into the negative half-wave of a slow oscillation. The first burst comes after the subject's own interval from that trough to the following up state, measured in an adaptation night (508 ms on average); the second follows 1,075 ms later, the slow oscillation's period; detection then pauses for 2.5 s. Stimulation runs for 210 minutes from about 5 minutes after the first stable stage 2 sleep, and halts outside stage 2 and slow-wave sleep and during arousals. Each of 11 subjects sleeps two experimental nights at least a week apart, in balanced order: one with stimulation, and a sham night in which the same detections are marked but no sound is played. In a separate control experiment, 7 other subjects receive the bursts out of phase: the first immediately at detection and the second about half a slow-oscillation period later (550 ms on average), tuned to the hyperpolarisation the first one causes. Recorded as a description of the published method; it asserts no effect."@en ;
    sstim:usesTechnique sstim-v:techClosedLoopAuditory ;
    sstim:intendedNeuralPhenomenon sstim-v:phenomenonOscillatoryDynamics ;
    sstim:participantEngagementMode sstim-v:engagementPassiveReceptive ;
    sstim:protocolStudyDesign sstim-v:designControlledTrial ;
    sstim:armAllocation sstim-v:allocationWithinSubject ;
    sstim:hasStudyPopulation n2013:population ;
    sstim:hasSchedule n2013:schedule ;
    sstim:hasStudyArm n2013:arm-in-phase, n2013:arm-sham, n2013:arm-out-of-phase ;
    sstim-ex:hasExposureProfile n2013:profile ;
    dct:source sstim-ref:NGO_2013 ;
    skos:editorialNote "Encoded from the full text (Neuron 78:545-553), Experimental Procedures, read 2026-10-15. Allocation is within subject: each stimulation condition is compared with its own sham night. The out-of-phase condition was a separate experiment on other subjects, compared with the in-phase one only between subjects. Four things the paper states have no SSTIM term yet, so they are in the description only: the interval between a detection's two bursts (1,075 ms in phase; individually tuned out of phase, 550 ms on average); the adaptive threshold (-80 microvolts by default, updated every 2 s to the most negative value of the preceding 5 s when that is lower); the in-phase trigger delay, set for each subject from an adaptation night, so no single delay is stated for that law; and the restriction of stimulation to stage 2 and slow-wave sleep. The sham night plays no sound, so it is a no-stimulation arm in SSTIM's terms, though the paper calls it sham. A third experiment (n = 4) that only moved the bursts 500 ms earlier is described in the paper and not encoded. The sound level was calibrated with a sound level meter, but the paper does not say where the level was measured."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    dct:created "2026-10-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:modified "2026-10-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .

n2013:population a sstim:PopulationDescriptor ;
    rdfs:label "Healthy young adults"@en ;
    dct:description "Eleven volunteers in the main experiment (eight women, three men, mean age 24.2 ± 0.9 years) and seven others in the out-of-phase control (five women, two men, 21.1 ± 0.7 years): native German speakers, free of medication, nonsmokers, with no neurological, psychiatric or sleep disorder and a regular sleep-wake rhythm."@en ;
    sstim:populationTaxon obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

# Two experimental nights per subject, one per condition; the adaptation night
# before them carries no stimulation and is not a session here.
n2013:schedule a sstim:StimulationSchedule ;
    sstim:sessionDurationSeconds "12600.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:sessionCount 2 .

n2013:arm-in-phase a sstim:StudyArm ;
    rdfs:label "Stimulation in phase with slow-oscillation up states"@en ;
    sstim:armRole sstim-v:armExperimental ;
    sstim:armStimulus n2013:stimulus .

n2013:arm-sham a sstim:StudyArm ;
    rdfs:label "Sham night: detections marked, no sound played"@en ;
    sstim:armRole sstim-v:armNoStimulation .

n2013:arm-out-of-phase a sstim:StudyArm ;
    rdfs:label "Stimulation out of phase with the slow-oscillation rhythm (separate control experiment)"@en ;
    sstim:armRole sstim-v:armActiveComparator ;
    sstim:armStimulus n2013:out-of-phase-stimulus .

n2013:profile a sstim-ex:ExposureProfile ;
    rdfs:label "Pink-noise bursts during non-REM sleep, timed by the sleeper's EEG"@en ;
    sstim-ex:usesStimulusChannel n2013:sound ;
    sstim-ex:hasKnowledgeStatus sstim-ex:knownInSSTIM .

n2013:sound a sstim-ex:StimulusChannel ;
    rdfs:label "In-ear headphones, both ears: 50 ms bursts of pink noise with 5 ms rise and fall"@en ;
    sstim-ex:deliveryMedium sstim-ex:mediumAirConductedSound ;
    sstim-ex:perceivedModality sstim-ex:modalityAuditory ;
    sstim-ex:hasBodyPlacement sstim-ex:placementEars ;
    sstim-ex:requiresDeviceCapability sstim-ex:capabilityHeadphones ;
    sstim-ex:hasStimulusPattern sstim-ex:patternPulsed, sstim-ex:patternAdaptive, sstim-ex:audioNoisePink ;
    sstim-ex:channelRole sstim-ex:roleIntendedIntervention ;
    sstim:hasMagnitude n2013:sound-level .

n2013:sound-level a sstim:StimulusMagnitude ;
    sstim:magnitudeQuantity sstim-v:quantitySoundPressureLevel ;
    sstim:magnitudeValue "55.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:magnitudeUnit sstim-v:unitDecibel ;
    sstim:deliveryStage sstim-v:stageUnstated ;
    sstim:valueBasis sstim-v:valueReported ;
    sstim:reportedAs "Sound volume was calibrated to 55 dB SPL using a Voltcraft sound level meter SL-400" .

n2013:stimulus a sstim:StimulusSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "Slow-oscillation phase-locked sound stimulation (Ngo et al. 2013)"@en ;
    sstim:stimulusRegime "adaptive" ;
    sstim:hasStimulusChannel n2013:sound ;
    sstim:hasControlLaw n2013:control-law ;
    sstim:hasStimulationTarget n2013:subject .

# Read the frontal EEG (Fpz against linked earlobes, 0.25 to 4 Hz), detect a
# slow oscillation's negative half-wave below the threshold, aim at the up
# state that follows, deliver two bursts, then ignore events for 2.5 s.
n2013:control-law a sstim:ControlLaw ;
    sstim:controlInputSignal sstim-v:measuredEeg ;
    sstim:trackedOscillation sstim-v:slowOscillation ;
    sstim:targetOscillationPhase sstim-v:phaseUpState ;
    sstim:detectionThresholdValue "-80.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:detectionThresholdUnit sstim-v:unitMicrovolt ;
    sstim:stimuliPerTrigger 2 ;
    sstim:refractoryPeriodSeconds "2.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:controlsChannel n2013:sound .

n2013:out-of-phase-stimulus a sstim:StimulusSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "Out-of-phase sound stimulation, separate control experiment (Ngo et al. 2013)"@en ;
    sstim:stimulusRegime "adaptive" ;
    sstim:hasStimulusChannel n2013:sound ;
    sstim:hasControlLaw n2013:out-of-phase-control-law ;
    sstim:hasStimulationTarget n2013:subject .

# The same detection, but the first burst at once, in the down state, and the
# second timed to the hyperpolarisation the first one evokes.
n2013:out-of-phase-control-law a sstim:ControlLaw ;
    sstim:controlInputSignal sstim-v:measuredEeg ;
    sstim:trackedOscillation sstim-v:slowOscillation ;
    sstim:targetOscillationPhase sstim-v:phaseDownState ;
    sstim:detectionThresholdValue "-80.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:detectionThresholdUnit sstim-v:unitMicrovolt ;
    sstim:triggerDelaySeconds "0.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:stimuliPerTrigger 2 ;
    sstim:refractoryPeriodSeconds "2.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:controlsChannel n2013:sound .

n2013:subject a bfo:0000040, obo:NCBITaxon_9606 ;
    rdfs:label "Sleeping human participant"@en .
